{"acceptance": ["Nothing is written to /mnt/netfs/ssd_pool/docker/user/host/owner/tofu or its worktrees; only read-only git commands are used against them", "A complete inventory table of unfinished work found there: branches, worktrees, lane refs, stashes, uncommitted changes, each with last commit, date, topic, whether it is already in this repo, and a continue/obsolete/duplicate recommendation", "Every unmerged branch and every piece of uncommitted work is imported into this repo as a branch under recovered/* (uncommitted work as a commit on its base) with no loss; verified by comparing commit SHAs and diff hashes", "Overlaps with the 9 in-flight tasks listed in the brief are flagged per item", "Inventory saved as a doc in the repo and summarized in the result"], "brief": "Owner message (2026-11-15): "你是从 /mnt/netfs/ssd_pool/docker/user/host/owner/tofu 这个路径拷贝过来的，那里其实有很多没完成的工作分支，但那个路径现在被写保护了，我没法操作。你看看能不能读取那里的信息，继续推进工作。" The current repo was copied from that old path. The old path is now write-protected, and it holds many unfinished work branches.

Do:
1. Read-only inventory of the OLD repo. Never write there: no git commands that touch its index, locks or refs. If git needs to write (for example index refresh), use `git --no-optional-locks`, set GIT_INDEX_FILE to a temporary copy, or read the objects directly. List local branches, refs/tofu/la", "idempotency_key": "opt-2026-11-15-recover-old-repo", "title": "Recover unfinished work branches from the old write-protected repo"}

